-- ============================================================
-- Warrior (Protection): Improved Disarm -> Blood and Thunder
-- ============================================================
-- TODO.md: "Improved Disarm (Renamed to Blood and Thunder) (1, 3): Redesigned.
--           When you Thunder Clap a target affected by Rend, you have a 50/100%
--           chance to Rend nearby enemies. (2 ranks)"
--
-- What it was: -10/-20 sec on Disarm's cooldown, and +5/10% damage taken while
-- disarmed.  Disarm does not work on the overwhelming majority of what a solo
-- warrior fights -- bosses and most elites are immune -- so both halves were
-- dead points in a tier you have to pass through.
--
-- The redesign gives Protection the one thing its AoE was missing: Thunder Clap
-- is a snap of damage with no follow-through, and Rend is a bleed nobody
-- maintains on more than one target because applying it costs a global each.
-- Joining them turns a pull into sustained area damage without adding a button.
--
-- The DBC half is minimal and deliberately so:
--
--   Effect1  SPELL_AURA_DUMMY, base points 50 / 100 -- the chance, read by the
--            script.  It is a dummy rather than a real aura because there is no
--            aura type for "a script may consult me".
--   Effect2  blanked (was the damage-taken-while-disarmed modifier).
--
-- Thunder Clap itself is untouched.  The script registers on -6343, i.e. all
-- ranks, and reads the chance off whichever talent rank the warrior has.
--
-- Why this needs C++: there is no generic DoT-spread mechanism anywhere in
-- core.  Every spell that does it -- Pestilence being the obvious one --
-- hand-rolls it in a script.  spell_warr_blood_and_thunder
-- (modules/world_of_alonecraft/src/WarriorBloodAndThunder.cpp) follows the
-- module's existing DK_Pestilence.cpp shape.  Its header explains the two
-- non-obvious decisions: the target list is snapshotted at selection time
-- because the Rend donor may be struck last, and the roll happens once per cast
-- rather than once per victim.
--
-- Rend is re-cast rather than copied, so core's spell_warr_rend
-- (src/server/scripts/Spells/spell_warrior.cpp:564) recalculates the periodic
-- damage from the warrior's weapon for each new target.  Crowd-controlled
-- enemies are skipped -- Rend is damage over time and would break them.
--
-- Spells:
--   12313 / 12804 = Blood and Thunder ranks 1-2 (was Improved Disarm)
--   6343          = Thunder Clap (rank 1; the script is registered on -6343)
--   772           = Rend (rank 1; the actual rank applied is whatever the
--                   donor is carrying)
-- ============================================================

